<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money rates see-saw, end higher.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money rates see-saw, end higher.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money rates fluctuated before closing up on Sunday as banks were unsure of the liquidity status, dealers said.</p>
<p>Overnight funds were initially traded at 17 to 19 percent as funds flowing in from maturing paper sold in an open market operation could not meet borrowing demand, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The market dipped to 15 percent and then again soared to the 19 percent mark near the close, the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
